  "ERROR PX": "ERROR PX",
  "Each edit is a config patch op at <code>/constraints/&lt;i&gt;/&lt;field&gt;</code> naming its constraint. Apply runs the installed producer (<code>rig --config</code>, then <code>check</code>) into a scratch build and reloads it under the same wind, gust and jolt state; Reset returns to the inspected build and clears the pending ops. Live preview changes strength, damping, inertia, wind, gravity and mix on the next evaluation; mass and component toggles require Apply. Clear resumes authored values without resetting integrated history.": "Each edit is a config patch op at <code>/constraints/&lt;i&gt;/&lt;field&gt;</code> naming its constraint. Apply runs the installed producer (<code>rig --config</code>, then <code>check</code>) into a scratch build and reloads it under the same wind, gust and jolt state; Reset returns to the inspected build and clears the pending ops. Live preview changes strength, damping, inertia, wind, gravity and mix on the next evaluation; mass and component toggles require Apply. Clear resumes authored values without resetting integrated history.",
  "Each edit is a config patch op at <code>/constraints/<i>/<field></code> naming its constraint. Apply runs the installed producer (<code>rig --config</code>, then <code>check</code>) into a scratch build and reloads it under the same wind, gust and jolt state; Reset returns to the inspected build and clears the pending ops. Live preview changes strength, damping, inertia, wind, gravity and mix on the next evaluation; mass and component toggles require Apply. Clear resumes authored values without resetting integrated history.": "Each edit is a config patch op at <code>/constraints/<i>/<field></code> naming its constraint. Apply runs the installed producer (<code>rig --config</code>, then <code>check</code>) into a scratch build and reloads it under the same wind, gust and jolt state; Reset returns to the inspected build and clears the pending ops. Live preview changes strength, damping, inertia, wind, gravity and mix on the next evaluation; mass and component toggles require Apply. Clear resumes authored values without resetting integrated history.",
  "Each edit is a config patch op at <code>/motion/tracks/&lt;i&gt;/…</code> or <code>/motion/blink/…</code>. Period is offered only among the divisors of <code>motion.duration</code> (the producer refuses any other, <code>CONFIG_PERIOD_DIVIDES_DURATION</code>). While edits are pending the preview drives the edited bones through the player's <code>adjust</code> with the producer's sine, <code>v(t) = base + amp·sin(2π(t/period − phase))</code>, on the bone the idle keys (<code>&lt;bone&gt;_ctl</code> under ctl keys); it is never recorded or submitted. Apply runs the installed producer (<code>rig --config</code>, then <code>check</code>) into a scratch build and replaces the preview with the built idle; Reset returns to the inspected build and clears the pending ops.": "Each edit is a config patch op at <code>/motion/tracks/&lt;i&gt;/…</code> or <code>/motion/blink/…</code>. Period is offered only among the divisors of <code>motion.duration</code> (the producer refuses any other, <code>CONFIG_PERIOD_DIVIDES_DURATION</code>). While edits are pending the preview drives the edited bones through the player's <code>adjust</code> with the producer's sine, <code>v(t) = base + amp·sin(2π(t/period − phase))</code>, on the bone the idle keys (<code>&lt;bone&gt;_ctl</code> under ctl keys); it is never recorded or submitted. Apply runs the installed producer (<code>rig --config</code>, then <code>check</code>) into a scratch build and replaces the preview with the built idle; Reset returns to the inspected build and clears the pending ops.",
  "Each edit is a config patch op at <code>/motion/tracks/<i>/…</code> or <code>/motion/blink/…</code>. Period is offered only among the divisors of <code>motion.duration</code> (the producer refuses any other, <code>CONFIG_PERIOD_DIVIDES_DURATION</code>). While edits are pending the preview drives the edited bones through the player's <code>adjust</code> with the producer's sine, <code>v(t) = base + amp·sin(2π(t/period − phase))</code>, on the bone the idle keys (<code><bone>_ctl</code> under ctl keys); it is never recorded or submitted. Apply runs the installed producer (<code>rig --config</code>, then <code>check</code>) into a scratch build and replaces the preview with the built idle; Reset returns to the inspected build and clears the pending ops.": "Each edit is a config patch op at <code>/motion/tracks/<i>/…</code> or <code>/motion/blink/…</code>. Period is offered only among the divisors of <code>motion.duration</code> (the producer refuses any other, <code>CONFIG_PERIOD_DIVIDES_DURATION</code>). While edits are pending the preview drives the edited bones through the player's <code>adjust</code> with the producer's sine, <code>v(t) = base + amp·sin(2π(t/period − phase))</code>, on the bone the idle keys (<code><bone>_ctl</code> under ctl keys); it is never recorded or submitted. Apply runs the installed producer (<code>rig --config</code>, then <code>check</code>) into a scratch build and replaces the preview with the built idle; Reset returns to the inspected build and clears the pending ops.",
  "Each reading is one <code>rigc render</code> of the drawn animation, on the inspected build and on the latest scratch build. Its frames become ticks under the timeline (<span class=\"tick-swatch inspected\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span> inspected, <span class=\"tick-swatch scratch\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span> scratch; click one to seek) and each pair gets its worst-frame line. A reading, not a gate: an unknown slot or bone is refused with rigc's own line.": "Each reading is one <code>rigc render</code> of the drawn animation, on the inspected build and on the latest scratch build. Its frames become ticks under the timeline (<span class=\"tick-swatch inspected\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span> inspected, <span class=\"tick-swatch scratch\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span> scratch; click one to seek) and each pair gets its worst-frame line. A reading, not a gate: an unknown slot or bone is refused with rigc's own line.",
