  "Put a pose sequence the package declares onto this rig: edit the <code>rig-pose-map/1</code> (per chain, the bone that carries each segment), set the clean and retarget flags, and Apply. The installed <code>@rig-c/pose</code> runs <code>rig-pose clean</code> and <code>rig-pose retarget</code> onto the handoff rig, and its <code>rigc</code> compiles the result, all into scratch; the new animation plays here beside the reference (pick the sequence under Reference). Review writes no keys and never writes the package's <code>motion.json</code>. Refusals (<code>POSE_NOT_CLEANED</code>, <code>POSE_BEND_ONE_WAY</code>, <code>RAISED_HEAD</code>, <code>MOTION_NAME_FREE</code>, <code>MAP_*</code>) are the producer's, verbatim. FEET, STANCE, FLIP, SHORT, END-ON, LEG-SCALE and REACH lines seek to their frame.": "Put a pose sequence the package declares onto this rig: edit the <code>rig-pose-map/1</code> (per chain, the bone that carries each segment), set the clean and retarget flags, and Apply. The installed <code>@rig-c/pose</code> runs <code>rig-pose clean</code> and <code>rig-pose retarget</code> onto the handoff rig, and its <code>rigc</code> compiles the result, all into scratch; the new animation plays here beside the reference (pick the sequence under Reference). Review writes no keys and never writes the package's <code>motion.json</code>. Refusals (<code>POSE_NOT_CLEANED</code>, <code>POSE_BEND_ONE_WAY</code>, <code>RAISED_HEAD</code>, <code>MOTION_NAME_FREE</code>, <code>MAP_*</code>) are the producer's, verbatim. FEET, STANCE, FLIP, SHORT, END-ON, LEG-SCALE and REACH lines seek to their frame.",
